              "rowSpan": 21
            }
          },
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "content": "Unity ships with basic pathfinding through NavMesh, but Overdawn's async, multi-scene levels needed much more. I indexed each scene with valid navigation points and built a NavigationManager that calculates paths across scenes using BFS, so NPCs and enemies can move through the world regardless of scene boundaries.<br><br>This same layer powers the transportation system that subways and elevators run on. It switches based on the player's currently active NavMesh, which determines which scene's behavior is active at any moment.",
            "variant": "body",
            "align": "left",
            "color": "foreground",
            "transform": "none"
          }
        },
