            "content": "The sequence system is event-driven for modularity, and dialogue runs through Yarn Spinner. Getting the authoring right, though, took me three full rewrites:<br><br><strong>v1: </strong>I started with a simple GameObject-based system, which quickly became unmanageable as sequences grew.<br><strong>v2:</strong> Then I built a graph with XNode for visual scripting. It was better, but Unity's IMGUI made it slow and unfriendly to use.<br><strong>v3:</strong> I finally landed on Unity 6's Behavior Tree. It was originally meant for character behaviors, but the model fit our actor-centric authoring far better — and designers finally gained real flexibility over individual actions.",
            "variant": "body",
            "align": "left",
            "color": "foreground",
            "transform": "none"
          }
        },
